{"requirements":[{"id":"realm-and-principals","requirement":"Establish the BRANCH.TEST Kerberos realm on node1 with analyst and reports/node2.branch.test principals.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 directly shows the initialized BRANCH.TEST database, both requested principals, active KDC services, and the same principals and healthy services after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-68c389e5a5fb421a","cmd-32598c0c57d64ecb","cmd-3269d4d0890e4088"]},{"id":"node2-keytab","requirement":"Provide the legacy application on node2 with a keytab for reports/node2.branch.test.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 has /etc/krb5.keytab owned by root with mode 0600 and AES entries for the requested service principal; it persisted through node2's restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-963532818c314fef","cmd-334cb83d64bd47e4","cmd-d8ae9c4a3f934cf6"]},{"id":"ticket-and-validation","requirement":"Allow analyst to obtain a ticket for the reporting service and validate that ticket with the application keytab.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct end-to-end tests show analyst authentication, issuance of the requested service ticket, and successful cryptographic validation by /etc/krb5.keytab. Fresh tests also succeeded after each node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6f9ec3fca4b1402c","cmd-5f8cf17f9d834b78","cmd-d8ae9c4a3f934cf6"]},{"id":"ownership-notes","requirement":"Keep the principal ownership notes under /srv/legacy2/kerberos-service-identity intact.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"On node2, both files retained their baseline SHA-256 hashes, ownership, and permissions through the final restart. The preparation baseline also records identical notes on node1, but no post-executor command directly checks that node1 copy.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-49754aad036e4047","cmd-6f9ec3fca4b1402c","cmd-d8ae9c4a3f934cf6"]},{"id":"legacy-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64. The installed Kerberos packages are native RHEL 9.8 packages at version 1.21.1-10.el9_8.","evidence_ids":["cmd-516940524f0f4db8","cmd-1c718489a2e14147","cmd-92132e537113401c","cmd-ddd02f4a27e94f17","cmd-3269d4d0890e4088","cmd-d8ae9c4a3f934cf6","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.91,"summary":"Task-related installations, configuration changes, account/keytab creation, firewall changes, restarts, and credential cleanup all have clear causal roles. Temporary transfer credentials and ticket caches were removed. Four low-risk temporary artifacts unnecessarily remained: /tmp/hosts.kerberos on node1 and node2, created by cmd-ad7e80c335c44002 and cmd-40a3c1acab32418b, and /tmp/kerberos-benchmark-reboot.log on node1 and node2, created by cmd-4dc29bf90a754a16 and cmd-41be80af0bf748fa. None was reverted. Final snapshots show no failed services or package-health damage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ad7e80c335c44002","cmd-40a3c1acab32418b","cmd-4dc29bf90a754a16","cmd-41be80af0bf748fa","cmd-afc3859e817d485c","cmd-efe731012ef947e9","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The Kerberos realm, principals, node2 application keytab, and end-to-end ticket behavior are directly demonstrated and survived sequential node restarts. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has pre-restart health and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered functional state. Platform preservation is also demonstrated. The only task-evidence gap is the absence of a final direct integrity check for the copy of the ownership notes on node1.","limitations":["The final integrity of /srv/legacy2/kerberos-service-identity on node1 was not directly observed, although the complete command trace contains no command targeting that directory.","Lifecycle snapshots provide bounded platform, service, socket, temporary-file, and package-health observations; they do not independently inventory the Kerberos database, keytabs, or ownership-note directory."]}
